# Which terminal xdg-terminal-exec(1) should open.
#
# xdg-terminal-exec is what the XDG spec says applications should call to open a
# terminal, and it is installed here. Its vendor list at
# /usr/share/xdg-terminal-exec/xdg-terminals.list still names foot and has no
# ghostty entry, so without this file it falls back to scanning every desktop
# entry with Categories=TerminalEmulator and picking one -- which is neither
# deterministic nor necessarily ghostty.
#
# ~/.config/xdg-terminals.list is the highest-priority location in the search
# path. Blank lines and #-comments are ignored; entries are Desktop Entry IDs.
com.mitchellh.ghostty.desktop
